  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Mantech Advanced Systems International obligated $750M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Mantech executed 120 awards for federal customers, with an average award size of $6.2M. Obligations fell 25.3% year over year. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, obligating $425M, followed by the Department of Defense with $243M. Other active buyers include the Department of the Interior with $20.4M and the Department of State with $17.9M. Computer Systems Design Services is the top market for Mantech, accounting for $382M in obligations. All Other Support Activities for Transportation and Engineering Services are the next largest markets, with $142M and $124M respectively. Smaller markets include Custom Computer Programming Services at $23.6M and Testing Laboratories and Services at $20.6M. FY2026 to date totals are partial. Historical context shows prior fiscal-year obligations of $901M in FY21, $1.1B in FY22, $884M in FY23, $1.2B in FY24, and $1B in FY25.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Mantech's FY2026 obligations among buyers?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration and the Department of Defense dominate FY2026 obligations. The General Services Administration obligated $425M and the Department of Defense obligated $243M, which together represent the majority of the $750M total. Remaining agencies include the Department of the Interior with $20.4M and the Department of State with $17.9M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product and service markets drive Mantech's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for Mantech at $382M. Support and engineering markets follow, with All Other Support Activities for Transportation at $142M and Engineering Services at $124M. Additional markets with notable obligations include Custom Computer Programming Services at $23.6M and Testing Laboratories and Services at $20.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
